<a name="overview"></a>
<font size=3><b>Overview</b></font></p>
Golf solitaire is played with a regular deck of cards dealt to seven piles with 5 cards face up in each pile.&nbsp; 
The total number of cards dealt is 35 leaving 17 cards in the stock.&nbsp; The object of the game is to move all of 
the cards from the tableau piles to the discard pile.&nbsp; Cards can only be moved one at a time and must be in 
ascending or descending sequence with the top-most card of the discard pile ( regardless of suit ).&nbsp; The cards 
are valued Ace low to King high.&nbsp; The sequence does not end at Ace and does not wrap to King.&nbsp; Therefore, 
it is only legal to move a '2' on to an Ace.&nbsp; Also, an Ace can be moved on to a '2'.&nbsp; A King can be played 
on a Queen but, the sequence ends there -- meaning a Queen cannot be played on a King.<p>   
As a program option, you can allow a Queen to be moved to a King by checking the checkbox,'Options : Customize' : 
'Allow Queen on King' .
<p>
<b>See also :</b>
<br>&nbsp;&nbsp; <a href="GolfSolitaire.htm#Options">Game Options</a>
<br clear=all>

<P>&nbsp;<!-- PegHelp --><hr><!-- *****Topic Break**** -->
<p><a name="Playing"></a><font size=3><b>Playing</b></font></p>
Play begins by either tapping the stock to reveal the first card in the deck or any of the top most cards in the tableau 
piles to move that card to the discard pile.&nbsp; The object of the game is to move all of the cards from the tableau 
piles to the discard pile.&nbsp; Cards can only be moved one at a time and must be in ascending or descending sequence 
with the top-most card of the discard pile ( regardless of suit ).&nbsp; The cards are valued Ace low to King high.&nbsp; 
The sequence does not end at Ace and does not wrap to King.&nbsp; Therefore, it is only legal to move a '2' on to an Ace.
&nbsp; Also, an Ace can be moved on to a '2'.&nbsp; A King can be played on a Queen but, the sequence ends there -- meaning 
a Queen cannot be played on a King.<p>   
Try to move as many cards from the tableau piles in ascending and 
descending sequence to the discard pile before dealing the next card.&nbsp; Your score is the number of cards left in the 
tableau piles after running through the hand.&nbsp; As with golf, the lower your score the better.
<p>
<b>See also :</b>
<br>&nbsp;&nbsp; <a href="GolfSolitaire.htm#Options">Game Options</a>
<br clear=all>

<P>&nbsp;<!-- PegHelp --><hr><!-- *****Topic Break**** -->
<p><a name="Options"></a><font size=3><b>Game Options</b></font></p>
From the menu, select 'Options : Customize' to set the game's difficulty and appearance.<p>
Select any of the 5 card styles or the '?' card to have the card style randomly selected before each game.&nbsp; 
<p>
When 'Allow Queen on King' is checked, you are allowed to play a Queen on a King.&nbsp; This is a variation of the rules 
which ends the sequence at King.

